# .dockerignore — allow-list of the Docker build context
#
# semantic-links:
#   skill-links:
#     - add-workspace-member
#   related-artifacts:
#     - Containerfile  # every COPY from the build context must be admitted below
#     - Cargo.toml  # every workspace member must be reachable for `cargo metadata`
#
# Policy (issue #2298): default-deny. Everything is excluded unless a rule below
# re-includes it. Forgetting a path fails the container build visibly; including
# a path by accident could ship unintended content, so no broad negations are used.
# The `recipe` stage runs `cargo chef prepare`, which calls `cargo metadata`; that
# requires every workspace member's manifest and declared target files to be
# present, so member crates are admitted whole.

*

# ── Cargo workspace ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
!/.cargo/
!/Cargo.toml
!/Cargo.lock
!/src/
!/tests/
!/packages/
!/console/

# ── Runtime data and container entry script (COPY ./share/) ───────────────────
!/share/

# ── C source compiled in the gcc stage (COPY ./contrib/dev-tools/su-exec/) ────
!/contrib/dev-tools/su-exec/

# ── Interim: AI-harness workspace members ─────────────────────────────────────
# These crates are explicit workspace members with no tracker dependency. They
# must be visible to `cargo metadata` but are not default members, so they are
# never compiled into container test archives. Remove each entry when the crate
# leaves the tracker workspace (EPIC #2003 harness-workspace sub-issue).
!/contrib/dev-tools/analysis/workspace-coupling/
!/contrib/dev-tools/checks/agent-review-report-contract/
!/contrib/dev-tools/checks/clippy-allow-reasons/
!/contrib/dev-tools/checks/frontmatter-validator/
!/contrib/dev-tools/checks/package-coverage-check/
!/contrib/dev-tools/github/github-review-threads/

# ── Re-exclusions inside admitted directories ─────────────────────────────────
# Agent instructions and package documentation are never read by a build stage.
**/AGENTS.md
**/docs/
